        "title": "HSK 4: form",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Family compounds are separate words with precise reference. A familiar component can guide recognition but cannot replace learning each compound’s relationship and reading.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "父母",
                "pinyin": "fùmǔ",
                "meaning": "father and mother; parents",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "1102198195c18c2accf517adf361e9660e75252476a0af6a39f3d5eed8d97419"
              },
              {
                "text": "父亲",
                "pinyin": "fùqīn",
                "meaning": "father",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "3deec0910d8e3ca838a86970f2d3db8403c3f0501597b4d73a8a38e00bdc6937"
              },
              {
                "text": "母亲",
                "pinyin": "mǔqīn",
                "meaning": "mother",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "974670f41dde707cf78872206abf553760904a146977b94e98612d7455e1dc3e"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A form has three distinct fields: both parents together, father only, and mother only. Match the complete family word to each field; a shared written part does not make the references identical.\nFamiliar meanings available: father and mother; parents; father; mother."
